          <baseCommit>f27f4850010526e8f3b9e07fae0a454b5c478cb4</baseCommit>
          <output>`Task.run` on `A02_01_UpdateDocSet` executed:

1. **Plan** — read `BmlDocSetPlan`: title &quot;BlockML Documentation&quot;, version &quot;0.1.0&quot;, summary (developer-handbook paragraph).
2. **Wipe** — live A02 data tree didn't exist yet, so no deletion needed.
3. **Packages** — created `a02_structuring/data`, `data/page`, `data/pagegroup`.
4. **Created** `packages/bmldocs/blocks/org/blockml/bml/bmldocs/a02_structuring/data/BmlDocSet_A02.bml`: baseType `docgen.core.DocSet`, title/summary/version overridden from the plan, `isNot` contrasting a single `DocPage` and `bmlcore:Documentation`, documentation naming that A02_02/A02_03 fill pages/homePage and pageGroups/rootPageGroup, `pages`/`pageGroups` declared empty, `homePage`/`rootPageGroup`/`learningPaths` omitted.
5. **Catalog** — `a02data:BmlDocSet_A02` was already exported in `Library.bml`, no change needed there.

Validated: same 6 pre-existing errors as baseline (unrelated stale catalog entries for later A02_02/A02_03 page/pagegroup work and old historical transform logs), no new errors introduced. Left git commits to the `transform apply` tooling, per the established `transform(operation-start)` → `transform(operation)` pattern seen in prior runs.</output>
